            <ArticleTitle>Duodenal diverticulum: incidental finding with potentially dangerous outcomes.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>56-57</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1080/20009666.2017.1291784</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present the case of an 83-year-old woman with a past medical history significant for schizoaffective disorder, presenting to our emergency department with the complaint of 'pain'. Given the non-specific complaint and the limited history obtained, CT imaging was performed on her chest and abdomen which incidentally found a large duodenal diverticulum. This manuscript discusses the incidence of duodenal diverticula and the potential associated complications.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
